@startuml MPOTA_Tile_Update
title MPOTA - tile source selection and self-hosted refresh

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFBFC
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #64748B
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  DiamondBorderColor #EA580C
  ArrowColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
}

start
if (Normal Docker development?) then (yes)
  :Use public OpenStreetMap tile endpoint;
  :Keep tile-bootstrap, tile-build,
and TileServer GL stopped;
  stop
else (self-hosted path)
  :Start Docker self-hosted profile\nor Kubernetes tile workload;
endif
:Start Docker Compose or Kubernetes tile workload;
:Read configured source URL, source file,
MBTiles file, checksum, required flag,
and refresh flag;

if (Tile file exists and
force refresh is false?) then (yes)
  :Keep the existing tile set;
  :Start TileServer GL read-only;
  stop
else (no)
  if (Tile source URL configured?) then (yes)
    :Download source to a temporary .part file
with retries and 5% progress logs;
    if (Source checksum valid when configured?) then (yes)
      if (Source is OSM PBF?) then (yes)
        :Convert PBF to OpenMapTiles-compatible
MBTiles with tilemaker and 5% progress logs;
      endif
    else (no)
      :Delete incomplete or invalid temporary file;
      :Fail the tile workload;
      stop
    endif
      if (Converted tile output valid?) then (yes)
        :Atomically move .part file
into the named volume or PVC;
        if (Development source was PBF?) then (yes)
          :Delete source PBF after successful extraction;
        endif
      :Write source/checksum/timestamp manifest;
      :Start TileServer GL read-only;
      stop
    else (no)
      :Delete incomplete or invalid temporary file;
      :Fail the tile workload;
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    if (Tile set required?) then (yes)
      :Fail the tile workload with configuration error;
      stop
    else (no)
      :Log that bootstrap was skipped;
      :Start TileServer GL for local development;
      stop
    endif
  endif
endif

note right
Normal Docker development uses the public OSM tile endpoint
with linked attribution and no local tile import.
Docker's self-hosted tile profile and Kubernetes production
use the artifact lifecycle below.
end note

note right
Docker: tile-bootstrap one-shot service + mpota-tile-data volume.
Kubernetes: tile-bootstrap init container + mpota-tiles PVC.
The artifact URL is deployment configuration because regional extracts
and licensed mirrors are selected outside the application repository.
end note
@enduml
